# Build trees. Each toolchain gets its own, and each installs into INSTALL inside itself.
build*/

# Compiler and linker output anywhere else, which is what a stray build in the source tree
# leaves behind.
*.obj
*.o
*.a
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.idb
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.wasm

# Assembled packages. Routine runs of the packaging script produce these constantly and
# they are rebuilt from source, so they are not worth committing.
#
# A package actually handed to somebody is worth committing, because that is the one thing
# source cannot reconstruct: a rebuild is functionally equivalent but not byte for byte,
# and from a later commit or a different toolset not even that. Add it deliberately when
# it happens:
#
#   git add -f dist/vgsdecoder-2.0.0
#
# Note that dist/vgsencoder-* carries the signing key inside the library. That is no new
# exposure - the key is in core/crypto/vgskeys.h as source - but it is one more reason
# this repository stays private.
dist/

# Editors and tools
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Captures and their by-products, far too large for a repository
*.mint
*.vgs
*.pgs
*.ply
